    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23615" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-occĭdŭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>never setting.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">axis,</span>”
				<i>the north pole</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					8, 175</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">visus,</span>”
				<i>ever open eyes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 6, 277</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignes,</span>”
				<i>inextinguishable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 3, 400</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vita continua et inoccidua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 68</span></i>
			.</div>
